	"children": [
		{
			"id": 1,
			"name": "AbstractAuditProviderService",
			"variant": "declaration",
			"kind": 128,
			"flags": {},
			"comment": {
				"summary": [
					{
						"kind": "text",
						"text": "An abstract class for Audit Module providers. Extend this class to store audit\nlogs somewhere other than the built-in providers.\n\nA provider only stores and reads audit logs. The Audit Module owns everything\naround it: validating recorded audit logs, assigning their IDs, buffering them,\nand retrying failed writes.\n\n### constructor\n\nThe constructor allows you to access resources from the module's container using the first parameter,\nand the provider's options using the second parameter.\n\n#### Example\n\n"
					},
					{
						"kind": "code",
						"text": "```ts\nimport { Logger } from \"@medusajs/framework/types\"\nimport { AbstractAuditProviderService } from \"@medusajs/framework/utils\"\n\ntype InjectedDependencies = {\n  logger: Logger\n}\n\ntype Options = {\n  url: string\n}\n\nclass MyAuditProviderService extends AbstractAuditProviderService {\n  static identifier = \"my-audit\"\n\n  protected logger_: Logger\n  protected options_: Options\n\n  constructor({ logger }: InjectedDependencies, options: Options) {\n    super()\n\n    this.logger_ = logger\n    this.options_ = options\n  }\n}\n\nexport default MyAuditProviderService\n```"
					}
				]
			},
			"children": [
				{
					"id": 2,
					"name": "identifier",
					"variant": "declaration",
					"kind": 1024,
					"flags": {
						"isStatic": true
					},
					"comment": {
						"summary": [
							{
								"kind": "text",
								"text": "Each audit provider has a unique identifier used to register it."
							}
						],
						"blockTags": [
							{
								"tag": "@example",
								"content": [
									{
										"kind": "code",
										"text": "```ts\nclass MyAuditProviderService extends AbstractAuditProviderService {\n  static identifier = \"my-audit\"\n  // ...\n}\n```"
									}
								]
							}
						]
					},
